# Opinion

Meeting: 0005-investigate-ssl-error-for-rps-arena-deployment
Agent: TestEngineer
Task: Investigate SSL error for RPS Arena deployment
Context:
  - Live host shows ERR_SSL_PROTOCOL_ERROR; we cannot hit it due to proxy 403 on CONNECT.
  - Server previously failed hard if MongoDB connection (MONGODB_URI) was unreachable, which would stop the listener entirely.
  - Workflow test failure highlighted missing healthCheckPath entries in .github/workflows/azure-containers.yml.
Position:
  - Treat resilience as testable behavior: bootstrap should fall back to in-memory on Mongo errors and surface JSON responses instead of crashing.
  - Workflow should keep explicit healthCheckPath strings so CI validates probe configuration.
Recommendations:
  - Add unit coverage for bootstrap paths (Mongo success, failure fallback, default responder) to maintain 100% coverage.
  - Reintroduce healthCheckPath="/healthz" and "/readyz" in the Azure workflow to satisfy tests and Azure probes.
  - Run npm test (c8 --100 node --test) and repo-level pytest --maxfail=1 to guard against regressions.
